window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>I wasn’t supposed to fall for a werewolf. He wasn’t supposed to break my heart. But he did—and I’m done letting ancient fairy tales decide my future.</p> <p>Sure, I’m named after the original Red Riding Hood (the real one, not the sanitized bedtime version), and yes, I was supposed to follow in her footsteps: master silver magic, protect the veil between humans and the supernatural, and become the next “wolf watcher” of the House of Red.</p> <p>But honestly? I’d rather eat dumplings and avoid werewolves altogether. That plan works… until Tobias Somfield shows up.</p> <p>He’s English. He’s brooding. He’s inconveniently heroic. And when he saves my life, I find myself pulled right back into the supernatural world I swore I was done with.</p> <p>All he wants is help hunting some rogue vampires. What we uncover? A centuries-old betrayal, a legend rewritten, and a legacy that might not be what it seems. If the truth doesn’t destroy us, it might just rewrite everything we thought we knew about reds, wolves—and each other.</p> <p>Smart, fast-paced, and packed with mythic twists, this urban fantasy adventure is perfect for fans of magical legacies, supernatural politics, and heroines who refuse to follow the rules.<br> <br> This collection contains the first three titles in the series:</p> <ul> <li><i>Requited</i></li> <li><i>Reluctant</i></li> <li><i>Relinquished</i></li> </ul>"; 
